diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index 3beff58..7c01546 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@ docs/                                          ← frame sheet and sprite (art s
 
 ## Rules
 
-- Frames are pixel art on a 32×32 grid. Never edit `mascot-frames.js` by hand; regenerate it from the drawing.
+- Frames are pixel art on a 48×48 grid, drawn in `docs/frames.py`. Never edit `mascot-frames.js`, the sprite or `frames.png` by hand; run `python3 docs/frames.py` (the sheet needs Pillow).
 - Motion is in steps only (`steps(1, end)`), never eased tweens, and nothing flashes. Keep the `prefers-reduced-motion` block in sync with any new animation.
 - State is classes on the `.nautas-mascot` element (`--look`, `--nod`, `--think`, `--wink`), set from DOM events. The search menu marks a running search with `.loading` on `.search-menu-container`; that is the only signal read from core.
 - The mascot is decorative: `aria-hidden`, no text of its own.
@@ -37,4 +37,6 @@ Add conventions and gotchas you discover to this file, in the same PR.
 - In `.gjs` templates a block param named like an HTML/SVG tag turns that tag into a component call: `{{#each paths as |path|}}<path />` crashes the whole search menu. Never name block params after tags.
 - QUnit does not load theme CSS, so `isVisible()` is meaningless there; assert the `hidden` attribute instead. On `/` only the welcome-banner search exists; the header field appears once the banner scrolls away.
 - System specs run with `Capybara.disable_animation`, so any frame shown only by a keyframe disappears in screenshots; the idle frame keeps `opacity: 1` at rest. On Horizon's `/` the search is the welcome-banner one.
+- anonist stands outside the field: on the top border in the welcome banner, left of it in the header. Horizon's header is 52 px, which fits the 48 px figure plus its 4 px hop; check it there after any size change.
+- Walk and hop durations live in both `common.scss` (`$walk-step`, `$hop-step`) and `MOVES` in the component; change them together.
 - To run CI locally: the `discourse/discourse_test:slim-browsers` image (what [dv](https://github.com/discourse/dv) builds on) with the steps of `discourse/.github`'s `discourse-theme.yml`; set `CI=1` so Chrome starts with `--no-sandbox`.
diff --git a/README.es.md b/README.es.md
index eb72de6..e97500b 100644
--- a/README.es.md
+++ b/README.es.md
@@ -12,11 +12,13 @@ Componente de tema para Discourse que pone a **anonist**, la mascota de la comun
 
 ## Qué hace
 
-anonist ocupa el lugar de la lupa y se mueve en pasos, estilo 8 bits:
+anonist se para junto al buscador, por fuera, y se mueve en pasos, estilo 8 bits. El buscador conserva su lupa.
 
 | Cuándo | Cuadro |
 |---|---|
 | No pasa nada | respira (sube un píxel) y pestañea cada tanto |
+| Al cargar y cada ~20 s, banner de bienvenida | camina sobre el borde superior del buscador y vuelve |
+| Al cargar y cada ~20 s, encabezado | salta tres pasos a la derecha, tres de vuelta y mira el buscador |
 | El buscador recibe foco | mira lo que escribes |
 | Haces una pausa al escribir | asiente un píxel |
 | La búsqueda está corriendo | piensa, con tres puntos que se encienden |
@@ -29,7 +31,7 @@ Con *reducir movimiento* activado en el sistema, queda quieta y solo cambia de c
 | Ajuste | Por defecto | Qué hace |
 |---|---|---|
 | `search_locations` | `header`, `welcome-banner` | Buscadores donde aparece la mascota |
-| `mascot_size` | `32` | Tamaño en píxeles; 32 es el tamaño del dibujo |
+| `mascot_size` | `48` | Tamaño en píxeles; 48 es el tamaño del dibujo |
 
 ## Instalación
 
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index d02306e..d84aa63 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -12,11 +12,13 @@ A Discourse theme component that puts **anonist**, the community mascot, in the
 
 ## What it does
 
-anonist takes the magnifier's place and moves in steps, 8-bit style:
+anonist stands next to the field, outside it, and moves in steps, 8-bit style. The field keeps its magnifier.
 
 | When | Frame |
 |---|---|
 | Nothing happens | breathes (up one pixel) and blinks now and then |
+| On load and every ~20 s, welcome banner | walks along the field's top border and back |
+| On load and every ~20 s, header | hops three steps right, three back, then looks at the field |
 | The field gets focus | looks at what you type |
 | You pause while typing | nods one pixel |
 | The search is running | thinks, with three dots lighting up |
@@ -29,7 +31,7 @@ With *reduce motion* turned on in the system, it stays still and only changes fr
 | Setting | Default | What it does |
 |---|---|---|
 | `search_locations` | `header`, `welcome-banner` | Search fields that show the mascot |
-| `mascot_size` | `32` | Size in pixels; 32 is the drawing's own size |
+| `mascot_size` | `48` | Size in pixels; 48 is the drawing's own size |
 
 ## Install
 
@@ -39,10 +41,10 @@ With *reduce motion* turned on in the system, it stays still and only changes fr
 
 | Path | Contents |
 |---|---|
-| `javascripts/discourse/lib/mascot-frames.js` | The six frames as pixel paths (generated, do not edit by hand) |
+| `javascripts/discourse/lib/mascot-frames.js` | The frames as pixel paths (generated by `docs/frames.py`, do not edit by hand) |
 | `javascripts/discourse/components/nautas-mascot.gjs` | Renders the frames and reads focus, typing and search state |
 | `common/common.scss` | Which frame shows in each state, and the step animations |
-| `docs/` | Frame sheet and SVG sprite, the drawing's source |
+| `docs/` | `frames.py`, the drawing's source (48×48 grids); it writes the frames, the SVG sprite and the frame sheet |
 
 ## License
 
diff --git a/common/common.scss b/common/common.scss
index c3ba8e3..8b3398a 100644
--- a/common/common.scss
+++ b/common/common.scss
@@ -1,29 +1,19 @@
 // Frames are stacked in one SVG; each state shows exactly one. Steps only, never tweens.
 $size: #{$mascot_size}px;
 $cycle: 6s;
+$px: calc(#{$size} / 48); // one pixel of the 48×48 drawing
+$walk-step: 0.16s; // keep $walk-step × 20 and $hop-step × 18 in sync with MOVES in the component
+$hop-step: 0.13s;
 
-// the mascot takes the magnifier's place
+// anonist stands outside the field, which keeps its own magnifier and spinner
 .search-input.nautas-mascot-host {
   position: relative;
-  padding-inline-start: calc(#{$size} + 0.8em);
-}
-
-.search-menu:has(.nautas-mascot-host) > .search-icon {
-  display: none;
-}
-
-// the mascot already shows the search is running
-.search-menu-container.loading .nautas-mascot-host > .searching:has(.spinner) {
-  display: none;
 }
 
 .nautas-mascot {
   position: absolute;
-  inset-block-start: 50%;
-  inset-inline-start: 0.4em;
   inline-size: $size;
   block-size: $size;
-  translate: 0 -50%;
   pointer-events: none;
   z-index: 1;
 
@@ -31,6 +21,19 @@ $cycle: 6s;
     display: none;
   }
 
+  // welcome banner: on the field's top border, at its left end
+  .search-input--welcome-banner & {
+    inset-block-end: calc(100% - #{$px});
+    inset-inline-start: 0.4em;
+  }
+
+  // header: left of the field, centred on it and 2 px low, so the 4 px hops stay inside
+  // the bar; 3 hops (24 px) reach the field's border
+  .search-input--header & {
+    inset-block-start: calc(50% - #{$size} / 2 + #{$px} * 2);
+    inset-inline-end: calc(100% + #{$px} * 16);
+  }
+
   &__art {
     display: block;
     inline-size: 100%;
@@ -76,7 +79,7 @@ $cycle: 6s;
   }
 
   &--look.nautas-mascot--nod .nautas-mascot__frame--look {
-    translate: 0 calc(100% / 32);
+    translate: 0 calc(100% / 48);
   }
 
   &--think {
@@ -114,7 +117,59 @@ $cycle: 6s;
     }
   }
 
+  // routines: walk in place (welcome banner), hop right and back (header)
+  &--walk,
+  &--hop {
+    .nautas-mascot__frame {
+      animation: none;
+      opacity: 0;
+    }
+  }
+
+  &--walk {
+    animation: nautas-mascot-walk $walk-step * 20 steps(1, end);
+
+    .nautas-mascot__frame--walk-a {
+      animation: nautas-mascot-slot-first-half $walk-step * 2 steps(1, end) 10;
+    }
+
+    .nautas-mascot__frame--walk-b {
+      animation: nautas-mascot-slot-half $walk-step * 2 steps(1, end) 10;
+    }
+  }
+
+  &--hop {
+    animation: nautas-mascot-hop $hop-step * 18 steps(1, end);
+
+    .nautas-mascot__frame--crouch,
+    .nautas-mascot__frame--air,
+    .nautas-mascot__frame--idle {
+      animation: nautas-mascot-slot-third $hop-step * 3 steps(1, end) 6;
+    }
+
+    .nautas-mascot__frame--air {
+      animation-delay: $hop-step;
+    }
+
+    .nautas-mascot__frame--idle {
+      animation-delay: $hop-step * 2;
+    }
+  }
+
   @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
+    &--walk,
+    &--hop {
+      animation: none;
+
+      .nautas-mascot__frame {
+        animation: none;
+      }
+
+      .nautas-mascot__frame--idle {
+        opacity: 1;
+      }
+    }
+
     &__frame--breathe,
     &__frame--blink {
       animation: none;
@@ -198,3 +253,71 @@ $cycle: 6s;
     opacity: 1;
   }
 }
+
+// shows a frame for the first half, first third or second half of each period
+@keyframes nautas-mascot-slot-first-half {
+  0% {
+    opacity: 1;
+  }
+
+  50% {
+    opacity: 0;
+  }
+}
+
+@keyframes nautas-mascot-slot-third {
+  0% {
+    opacity: 1;
+  }
+
+  33.333% {
+    opacity: 0;
+  }
+}
+
+@keyframes nautas-mascot-slot-half {
+  0% {
+    opacity: 0;
+  }
+
+  50% {
+    opacity: 1;
+  }
+}
+
+// 10 steps of 4 px right along the top border, then 10 back
+@keyframes nautas-mascot-walk {
+  @for $i from 0 through 19 {
+    #{$i * 5%} {
+      translate: calc(#{$px} * #{if($i <= 10, $i, 20 - $i) * 4}) 0;
+    }
+  }
+
+  100% {
+    translate: 0 0;
+  }
+}
+
+// 6 hops of 8 px (crouch, air, land): 3 right, 3 back
+@keyframes nautas-mascot-hop {
+  @for $i from 0 through 5 {
+    $dir: if($i < 3, 1, -1);
+    $x: if($i < 3, $i * 8, (6 - $i) * 8);
+
+    #{$i * 3 * 5.5556%} {
+      translate: calc(#{$px} * #{$x}) 0;
+    }
+
+    #{($i * 3 + 1) * 5.5556%} {
+      translate: calc(#{$px} * #{$x + 4 * $dir}) calc(#{$px} * -4);
+    }
+
+    #{($i * 3 + 2) * 5.5556%} {
+      translate: calc(#{$px} * #{$x + 8 * $dir}) 0;
+    }
+  }
+
+  100% {
+    translate: 0 0;
+  }
+}
